& [PrototypeDevelopmentPolicy] governs reversible exploratory development
  + [PDP-001] preserve raw specification source before synthesis
  + [PDP-002] select the smallest high-leverage identity or novel seam that can falsify the architecture
  + [PDP-003] draw a basic feature flowchart and describe every node before defining execution
  + [PDP-004] graduate each flowchart node into typed inputs outputs transforms gates states faults and trace
  + [PDP-005] implement only the smallest end-to-end executable slice
  + [PDP-006] run positive negative and control cases and preserve inspectable evidence
  + [PDP-007] iterate abandon or promote only from observed evidence
  = must: use the lowest sufficient governance ramp while preserving source lineage boundary integrity and falsifiability
  = must: keep experimental outputs distinct from trusted authority
  = should: prefer one vertical workflow over many disconnected components
  - never: require near-release completeness before a reversible proof of concept can run
  - never: promote a passing prototype beyond the authority explicitly signed here

& [FeatureFlowchart] is the basic flow with node descriptions
  + [F0 PreservedSource] captures intent and constraints without reinterpretation
  + [F1 StimulusIntake] accepts one bounded user command and assigns a trace identity
  + [F2 FirstInference] asks llama.cpp to choose exactly one route_attention call for routed cases
  + [F3 CallValidation] rejects any wrong missing extra or malformed call before tool execution
  + [F4 CantorSubroutine] invokes the pinned read-only MCP adapter with response_mode frame
  + [F5 ResultAdmission] admits a typed positive frame or typed refusal as evidence not authority
  + [F6 ReflectionInference] supplies the exact result to a separate second llama.cpp request
  + [F7 FinalValidation] requires structured output that acknowledges tool status and evidence identity or fault
  + [F8 TraceAndDecision] preserves a replayable trace and yields pass fail or control
  + [flow] is F0 -> F1 -> F2 -> F3 -> F4 -> F5 -> F6 -> F7 -> F8
  + [control_flow] is F0 -> F1 -> F2_control -> F7_control -> F8

& [ProgramExecutionFlow] is the graduated executable state machine
  + [state_set] is created first_inference_requested tool_call_received tool_call_validated tool_result_received reflection_requested final_received completed failed or control_completed
  + [routed_transition_1] is created plus Stimulus to first_inference_requested
  + [routed_transition_2] is one exact model tool call to tool_call_received
  + [routed_transition_3] is host schema validation to tool_call_validated
  + [routed_transition_4] is MCP response to tool_result_received
  + [routed_transition_5] is exact tool evidence projection to reflection_requested
  + [routed_transition_6] is schema-valid model response to final_received then completed
  + [failure_transition] is any rejected precondition to failed with a typed fault and no invented successor state
  + [control_transition] is created to one no-tools provider request to final validation then control_completed

& [DataContract] is the executable externalized frame
  + [Stimulus] has trace_id case_id text and expected_case_kind
  + [SubroutineCall] has call_id name and closed arguments stimulus plus response_mode
  + [SubroutineResult] has structured_content is_error and observed_status
  + [FinalOutput] has case_id observed_tool_status applied_attention summary and evidence_reference
  + [ExecutionTrace] has profile trace_id case_id expected_case_kind final_state ordered_events sanitized requests sanitized responses tool_call tool_result final_output and fault
  = must: reject unknown contract fields where the host owns the schema
  = must: sanitize provider-private reasoning fields recursively before persistence

& [ImplementationSliceP0] is the isolated Rust proof
  + [provider] is the already-running unmodified EVO-X2 llama.cpp server on loopback
  + [model] is the model advertised by GET /v1/models at run time
  + [tool] is the already-deployed cantor-attention-mcp executable over STDIO MCP
  + [case_positive] asks about Cantor and requires route_selected plus a reflected procedure identifier
  + [case_refusal] asks for an unsupported Weaver route and requires runtime_refused to remain explicit
  + [case_control] asks for a direct bounded response with no tool offered and records control_completed
  + [call_bound] is one tool call maximum
  + [pass_bound] is two llama.cpp requests for routed cases and one for control
  + [effect_boundary] is read-only semantic routing and evidence writing only
  = must: run without modifying or restarting llama.cpp
  = must: spawn the MCP adapter ephemerally and leave no persistent adapter process
  = must: preserve the deployed adapter and runtime hashes in evidence

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [CRLP-001] preserved source manifest and this SJS signature verify
  + [CRLP-002] feature descriptions map one-to-one into execution states or deliberate non-runtime policy nodes
  + [CRLP-003] deterministic tests cover exact call malformed call multiple call positive result refusal result final schema and private-field sanitization
  + [CRLP-004] positive live run emits one valid call invokes real route_attention imports its verified frame into pass two and cites its evidence reference
  + [CRLP-005] refusal live run imports and states the real refusal without a positive frame or fabricated route
  + [CRLP-006] control live run invokes no Cantor tool and is distinguishable from routed success
  + [CRLP-007] every case yields an ordered replayable sanitized trace
  + [CRLP-008] llama.cpp remains the same process and the adapter remains ephemeral

& [AuthorityBoundary] is experimental implementation authority
  + permits one isolated P0 implementation tests deployment copy live execution evidence and defect repair
  + excludes trusted catalogue mutation autonomous effects Codex registration provider restart nested procedures and general production claims
  + learned routing results remain evidence-backed proposals

